# Copy to `.env` and fill in the keys. `.env` is already in `.gitignore`.
#
# Two groups: **thinking** (LLM) and **speaking** (TTS). Listening is always the
# browser's Web Speech API — no variable here changes that.
#
# No `VITE_` prefix, on purpose: variables with that prefix are baked straight
# into the bundle that runs on the user's machine. The keys here are only read
# by the routes in `server/` and never reach the browser. `pnpm dev` loads this
# file automatically; on Vercel, set the same variables under Project Settings →
# Environment Variables.
#
# The app **still runs** without keys: the LLM falls back to a model running on
# the machine's GPU, and speech falls back to the operating system's vi-VN voice.

# ── LLM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Get a key at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Without a key the Settings screen says so right away and you pick an
# on-device model — marked `(on-device)` — from the list. The first turn is slow
# because the weights have to download, but no network is needed after that.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Default model for the cloud path. Must be in the allowlist in
# `src/llm/openai-models.ts` — the proxy rejects any name outside that list.
#
# `gpt-4.1-mini` is the default because this problem is bound by **latency to
# the first tool call**: the 4.1 family has no thinking phase, while `nano`
# falls short on the genuinely hard part, direction-flip ("lạnh quá" — "so
# cold" — must give `warmer`). Don't change it because of a benchmark table —
# change it when the eval suite produces numbers.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini

# Point at another OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Azure, self-hosted vLLM, OpenRouter…).
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# ── Voice ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Get a key at https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Defaults to `eleven_v3_conversational` — pronounces Vietnamese tones
# correctly, nearly as fast as Flash. `eleven_flash_v2_5` is a little faster but
# sounds more foreign-accented. `eleven_multilingual_v2` doesn't speak
# Vietnamese.
# TTS_MODEL=eleven_v3_conversational

# A **voice_id**, not the speaker's name. Must be a *default* voice or one you
# created in your account — voices taken from the voice library return 402 on
# the free tier.
# Usable defaults: EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL (Sarah), cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9 (Jessica),
#                  JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb (George), pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku (Lily)
# TTS_VOICE=cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9

# ── Music ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# YouTube Data API v3 key — create one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# then enable "YouTube Data API v3" for that project.
# Only used to **search** for songs (`/api/music/search`). Playback runs through
# the YouTube iframe and needs no key: without a key the default playlist in
# `src/music/catalog.ts` still plays.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# ── Web lookup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Tavily key at https://app.tavily.com — the free plan has 1,000 credits/month
# (one search costs 1, reading 5 pages costs 1). Powers the two cloud-path tools
# `web_search` and `web_fetch` (`/api/web/*`): weather, news, prices… Without a
# key the car still works normally and just says it can't look things up. The
# on-device model doesn't have these two tools.
TAVILY_API_KEY=
